# A playable tour of the current BunNarraY language.
# Run it more than once to explore the alternate options. Every route rejoins
# the main tour, except the explicit replay choice near the end.
# The playground needs no initial memory; all values are set in this file.
# Authored by ChatGPT Sol.

:SPEAKER Curator
Welcome to the Clockwork Archive.
This placard literally reads &lbrack;open&rbrack; &lbrace;carefully&rbrace; &hash;1.
To print the escape itself, write &amp;lbrace; in the source.
This sentence has a public ending. # This part is only a source comment.

# A blank name in an alternating speaker list means the narrator.
:ALTERNATE Curator; ; Clockwork Guide
I will introduce the exhibits.
The gears turn overhead.
Please keep your hands inside the story.
:ALTERNATE
I am still the Clockwork Guide after the rotation stops.
:SPEAKER
The narrator takes over again.

:SET visitor=traveler
:SET mood=curious
:SET key=missing
:SET route=unset
:SET souvenir=none

Choose a name for your admission card. {
    ?: [id:card_ada] Ada
        :SET visitor=Ada
        :SIGNAL card_written:Ada
    ?: [id:card_bo] Bo
        :SET visitor=Bo
        :SIGNAL card_written:Bo
}
Welcome, $visitor. The admission card now shows your name.

# The first matching branch wins. Both conditions below are true.
:SET first_lamp=lit
:SET second_lamp=lit
[branch]
    [when:first_lamp=lit]
        The first lamp lights the hall.
        :SIGNAL first_lamp
    [when:second_lamp=lit]
        The second lamp would speak only if the first were dark.
[/branch]

# An unmatched branch falls through without speaking.
[branch]
    [when:missing_exhibit=found]
        This line is unreachable with the memory set above.
[/branch]
We arrive at the display cases.

# Both [when] and [id] orders are accepted on individual options.
# The plain option stays visible for every memory state.
How should we inspect the first cabinet? {
    ?: [when:mood=curious] [id:look_close] Look closely
        :SPEAKER Curator
        The latch is shaped like a small moon.
        :SPEAKER
        :SET key=brass
        :SIGNAL key_found:brass
    ?: [id:ask_guide] [when:mood=curious] Ask the guide
        :ALTERNATE Curator; Clockwork Guide
        Is that a key beneath the glass?
        Yes. I will lift the cover for you.
        :ALTERNATE
        :SET key=brass
    ?: [id:walk_past] Walk past
        We leave the key where it is.
}
All three cabinet answers rejoin here; your key is $key.

# Prompted nested options, with a branch and a yield inside one answer.
Which mechanism shall we try next? {
    ?: [id:music_box] The music box
        Which tune? {
            ?: [id:waltz] A waltz
                :SET tune=waltz
                :YIELD wind_box:waltz
                The box plays a $tune for $visitor.
            ?: [id:march] A march
                :SET tune=march
                :SIGNAL music_started:march
                The brass drummer keeps time.
        }
        The music box closes, whichever tune you chose.
    ?: [id:telescope] The telescope
        # A bare nested choice has no new spoken prompt.
        {
            ?: [id:near] Focus nearby
                :SET focus=near
                A brass rabbit fills the lens.
            ?: [id:far] Focus far away
                :SET focus=far
                A distant observatory comes into view.
        }
        [branch]
            [when:focus=near]
                The rabbit waves at $visitor.
            [when:focus=far]
                The observatory beacon flashes twice.
        [/branch]
    ?: [id:sealed_drawer] The sealed drawer
        [branch]
            [when:key=brass]
                The brass key fits.
                :SIGNAL drawer_opened
            [when:key=missing]
                Without a key, we leave it sealed.
        [/branch]
}
We meet again at the center of the gallery.

# Adjacent choice blocks chain without a fresh prompt. The first answer sets
# memory for the second, and both answers fall into the shared line.
Choose a souvenir, then a wrapping. {
    ?: [id:gear] A tiny gear
        :SET souvenir=gear
    ?: [id:map] A folded map
        :SET souvenir=map
} {
    ?: [id:paper] Brown paper
        :SET wrapping=paper
    ?: [id:ribbon] Blue ribbon
        :SET wrapping=ribbon
}
Your $souvenir arrives with $wrapping.

# A yield separates this spoken prompt from its bare choice. Conditional
# options are checked when the visitor resumes from the yield.
The route display is about to light up.
:YIELD reveal_routes:gallery
{
    ?: [when:key=brass] [id:locked_stair] Unlock the spiral stair
        :SET route=stair
        :SIGNAL route_chosen:stair
    ?: [id:bridge] Cross the bridge
        :SET route=bridge
    ?: [id:lift] Take the lift
        :SET route=lift
}

# An option may lead to a branch, which may lead to another choice.
[branch]
    [when:route=stair]
        The key turns in the stairwell door.
        [branch]
            [when:key=brass]
                A second lock opens too.
                :YIELD climb_stairs
        [/branch]
    [when:route=bridge]
        The bridge sways under $visitor.
        Do you stop at the midpoint? {
            ?: [id:pause] Yes
                :SIGNAL bridge_photo
                We take in the view.
            ?: [id:continue] No
                We keep walking.
        }
    [when:route=lift]
        The lift rattles to the top floor.
[/branch]
Every route reaches the observatory.

# Every option in this choice is hidden. The VM skips the empty option list
# and continues to the next line after speaking the prompt.
The closed midnight exhibit has no available entrances. {
    ?: [when:hour=midnight] Enter the moon room
        This answer cannot appear in a normal run.
    ?: [when:permit=gold] Enter the star room
        Neither can this one.
}
We continue past the closed exhibit without selecting anything.

# This branch mixes two memory values. A brass key takes the first case even
# on the lift route; its nested branch can then miss and fall through.
[branch]
    [when:key=brass]
        [branch]
            [when:route=stair]
                The key and the stair route reveal a hidden constellation.
            [when:route=bridge]
                The key glints over the bridge chart.
        [/branch]
    [when:route=lift]
        The lift ticket unlocks an upper shelf.
[/branch]
The observatory clock strikes once.

# SET without a value deletes a variable. A missing variable interpolates as
# an empty string, so the final pair of brackets below is empty.
:SET temporary=ink
The temporary mark is $temporary.
:SET temporary
The temporary mark is now &lbrack;$temporary&rbrack;.

# A choice can jump forward into a skip block. Linear execution skips it.
Would you like the optional attic tour? {
    ?: [id:attic] Yes, show me
        ->attic
    ?: [id:stay] Stay in the observatory
        The curator nods and leaves the attic closed.
}
->after_attic
[skip:attic]
    :SPEAKER Curator
    Only curious visitors see this hidden room.
    :SIGNAL attic_entered
    :YIELD unfold_attic_ladder
    The ledger names $visitor as today's explorer.
    :SPEAKER
    ->after_attic
[/skip]
@after_attic
The tour ends beside the great clock.

# The backward goto replays the last choice; the other answer reaches END.
@last_chance
Shall we check the clock once more? {
    ?: [id:again] Yes, repeat this question
        ->last_chance
    ?: [id:finish] No, finish the tour
        :SIGNAL tour_complete
}
Goodbye, $visitor.
